00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:52.100
So it's creating content from
content 'cause you're busy

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:53.290
and you're one person.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.240
So there's an efficiency
of content production

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:57.930
from a masterpiece of content
that creates collateral,

00:13:57.930 --> 00:13:59.910
that makes the volume
that you're looking for

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:03.560
more palpable than, it's more
documenting than creating.

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:06.530
Which as you can imagine
makes it a lot easier

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.920
'cause the creating part
is what holds people back.

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:11.770
- [Woman] And say the constant
debate we have at work--

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:12.603
- Yes.

00:14:12.603 --> 00:14:14.530
- [Woman] Is what should
frequency strategy be?

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:16.050
Can you involve people too much?

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:17.490
Do they really get annoyed?

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:19.422
Do they even remember your ads
when they see it three times?

00:14:19.422 --> 00:14:21.090
What's your opinion?

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:23.043
- So, I think it comes down to,

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.540
it comes down to what
you're bombarding them with.

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:28.610
Can the New York Jets bombard me too much?

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:30.931
Absolutely not, bombard away.

00:14:30.931 --> 00:14:34.723
Can Milky Way candy bars
bombard me too much?

00:14:34.723 --> 00:14:37.070
They sure can 'cause
I don't really like it

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:40.045
or consider it, but if
their creative is clever,

00:14:40.045 --> 00:14:42.560
or utilitarian, or interesting.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.260
What about more importantly
if they gave me four different

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:47.120
